:   - Placement and refund logic\n1067:   - Phase-based behavior\n1068: - [ ] Write unit tests for movement detection\n1069:   - Connected component detection\n1070:   - Centroid tracking\n1071:   - Classification accuracy\n1072: - [ ] Write unit tests for scoring system\n1073:   - Score calculation accuracy\n1074:   - Score cap handling\n1075:   - High score persistence\n1076: - [ ] Write unit tests for level progression\n1077:   - Level configuration generation\n1078:   - Difficulty scaling\n1079: - [ ] Write integration tests\n1080:   - End-to-end game flow\n1081:   - Level progression\n1082:   - Score calculation\n1083:   - UI interaction\n1084: - [ ] Add manual testing procedures\n1085:   - Mobile responsiveness\n1086:   - Touch interaction\n1087:   - Audio on different browsers\n1088:   - Performance with high cell counts\n1089:   - Accessibility testing\n1090: \n1091: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n1092: \n1093: ### 6.5 Documentation (LOW - Knowledge Transfer)\n1094: \n1095: - [ ] Write README.md\n1096:   - Project overview\n1097:   - Installation instructions\n1098:   - Controls and gameplay guide\n1099:   - Configuration options\n1100:   - Known issues and limitations\n1101: - [ ] Add code comments\n1102:   - Complex algorithms (movement detection, simulation)\n1103:   - State machine logic\n1104:   - Performance-critical sections\n1105: - [ ] Document API interfaces\n1106:   - Component props\n1107:   - Utility functions\n1108:   - Configuration schemas\n1109:   - Type definitions\n1110: - [ ] Create developer guide\n1111:   - Architecture overview\n1112:   - How to add new features\n1113:   - Debugging tips\n1114:   - Common patterns\n1115: - [ ] Document expert settings\n1116:   - Each parameter explanation\n1117:   - Recommended values\n1118:   - Impact on gameplay\n1119: \n1120: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n1121: \n1122: ---\n1123: \n1124: ## Parallel Development Tracks\n1125: \n1126: ### Track A (Can start after Project Setup):\n1127: \n1128: - Type definitions → Shared utilities → All other systems\n1129: \n1130: ### Track B (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1131: \n1132: - Phase Management → UI Overlay → Phase Status Display\n1133: - Canvas Rendering → Grid Interaction\n1134: \n1135: ### Track C (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1136: \n1137: - User Interaction → Audio Sonification → Visual Polish\n1138: - Flux Management → Grid Interaction\n1139: \n1140: ### Track D (Can start after Canvas Rendering + User Interaction + Flux Management):\n1141: \n1142: - Grid Integration → Playable MVP\n1143: \n1144: ### Track E (Can start after MVP):\n1145: \n1146: - Intro Overlay → Main UI Controls → Settings Panel\n1147: - Movement Detection → Scoring System → Level Progression\n1148: \n1149: ### Track F (Can start after Level Progression):\n1150: \n1151: - Transition System → Victory Screen\n1152: \n1153: ### Track G (Can start after Scoring + Level Progression):\n1154: \n1155: - Audio Sonification → Visual Polish → Mobile Enhancements\n1156: \n1157: ### Track H (Can start after all features):\n1158: \n1159: - Expert Settings → Presets → Error Handling → Accessibility → Performance → Testing → Documentation\n1160: \n1161: ---\n1162: \n1163: ## Critical Path (Sequential Must-Haves for MVP):\n1164: \n1165: 1. **Project Setup** → Build system\n1166: 2. **Type Definitions** → All type-safe development\n1167: 3. **Shared Utilities** → Validation and state management\n1168: 4. **Simulation Engine** → Core gameplay logic\n1169: 5. **Phase Management with COUNTDOWN** → Game flow control\n1170: 6. **Canvas Rendering** → Visual feedback\n1171: 7. **User Interaction** → Input handling\n1172: 8. **Flux Management** → Resource system\n1173: 9. **Grid Integration** → Playable MVP\n1174: \n1175: ## Testing Milestones:\n1176: \n1177: - **After Sprint 1**: MVP manually playable (place cells, watch simulation, all phases work)\n1178: - **After Sprint 2**: Full game UI (intro, controls, scoring, settings)\n1179: - **After Sprint 3**: Complete game loop (intro → levels → transitions → victory)\n1180: - **After Sprint 4**: Audio and polish (all sounds, visual enhancements, mobile support)\n1181: - **After Sprint 5**: Expert settings and customization\n1182: - **After Sprint 6**: Production-ready with stability, accessibility, performance, tests, and docs\n1183: \n1184: ## Success Criteria:\n1185: \n1186: - [ ] Playable MVP after Sprint 1 (can place cells and run simulation with all phases)\n1187: - [ ] Complete UI after Sprint 2 (intro, controls, settings)\n1188: - [ ] Full game loop after Sprint 3 (intro → levels → scoring → transitions → victory)\n1189: - [ ] Audio and polish after Sprint 4 (all sounds, animations, mobile support)\n1190: - [ ] All features implemented after Sprint 5 (expert settings, presets)\n1191: - [ ] Production-ready after Sprint 6 (stability, accessibility, performance, tests, docs)\n1192: - [ ] 60fps performance with 500+ cells\n1193: - [ ] Works on mobile and desktop\n1194: - [ ] Audio works across all major browsers\n1195: - [ ] No console errors or warnings in production\n1196: - [ ] High score persistence works\n1197: - [ ] Expert settings properly configure all systems\n1198: - [ ] All critical edge cases handled gracefully\n1199: - [ ] Accessible keyboard navigation\n1200: - [ ] Comprehensive test coverage for core systems\n1201: - [ ] Clear documentation for developers and players\n1202: \n1203: ## Framework Decisions (MAKE THESE FIRST):\n1204: \n1205: - **Framework**: React/Vite (recommended for performance and DX)\n1206: - **State Management**: React hooks (useState, useReducer, useRef) - minimal, no external library needed\n1207: - **Styling**: CSS modules or vanilla CSS with CSS variables for theming\n1208: - **Testing**: Vitest (fast, compatible with Vite)\n1209: - **Build Tool**: Vite (recommended for speed and simplicity)\n1210: \n1211: ## Implementation Order Recommendations:\n1212: \n1213: ### Week 1: Foundation\n1214: \n1215: 1. Project setup (Day 1)\n1216: 2. Type definitions (Day 1)\n1217: 3. Shared utilities (Day 2)\n1218: 4. Simulation engine (Day 2-3)\n1219: 5. Phase management with COUNTDOWN (Day 3-4)\n1220: 6. Canvas rendering (Day 4)\n1221: \n1222: ### Week 2: Interaction & UI\n1223: \n1224: 7. User interaction (Day 1)\n1225: 8. Flux management (Day 1-2)\n1226: 9. Grid interaction (Day 2) - MVP milestone reached\n1227: 10. Intro overlay (Day 3)\n1228: 11. Main UI controls (Day 3-4)\n1229: 12. Phase status display (Day 4)\n1230: \n1231: ### Week 3: Scoring & Progression\n1232: \n1233: 13. Movement detection (Day 1-2)\n1234: 14. Scoring system (Day 2-3)\n1235: 15. Settings panel (Day 3)\n1236: 16. Level progression (Day 4)\n1237: \n1238: ### Week 4: Transitions & Audio\n1239: \n1240: 17. Transition system (Day 1-2)\n1241: 18. Victory screen (Day 2)\n1242: 19. Audio sonification (Day 3-4)\n1243: 20. Visual polish (Day 4)\n1244: \n1245: ### Week 5: Advanced Features\n1246: \n1247: 21. Expert settings (Day 1-3)\n1248: 22. Mobile enhancements (Day 3)\n1249: 23. Presets system (Day 4)\n1250: \n1251: ### Week 6: Quality Assurance\n1252: \n1253: 24. Error handling (Day 1)\n1254: 25. Accessibility (Day 1-2)\n1255: 26. Performance optimization (Day 2)\n1256: 27. Testing (Day 3-4)\n1257: 28. Documentation (Day 4)\n1258: \n1259: ## Notes:\n1260: \n\n(Output truncated at 51200 bytes. Use 'offset' parameter to read beyond line 1260)\n</content>","title":"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation Plan\n\nThis plan prioritizes building a playable, enjoyable game first, then incrementally enhances with advanced features. All requirements from 14 specification files are included with proper dependencies and priorities.\n\n---\n\n## Sprint 1: Foundation (MVP Core)\n\n_Goal: Basic Game of Life with visualization, interaction, and game flow_\n\n### 1.1 Project Setup & Build System (CRITICAL - FIRST PRIORITY)\n\n- [x] Choose and initialize framework (React/Vite recommended for perf