{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771183111346,"sessionID":"ses_39d430eecffenagK7FExfhPqyr","part":{"id":"prt_c62bd07110016HlC7vMfG1XVdi","sessionID":"ses_39d430eecffenagK7FExfhPqyr","messageID":"msg_c62bcf1f2001dzebSktXGBwYyR","type":"tool","callID":"call_d410362c908d446fa5b89675","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Study specs directory comprehensively","prompt":"Study all files in specs/ directory to understand the application specifications. I need you to:\n1. Read all specification files in specs/*\n2. Identify all features, requirements, and specifications\n3. Note any relationships between different specifications\n4. Provide a comprehensive summary of what needs to be implemented\n\nBe very thorough - this is critical for understanding the application requirements.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39d42f8dbffexRcfuMGBTaER7I (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n# Comprehensive Application Specifications Analysis\n\nI've thoroughly studied all 12 specification files in the specs/ directory. Here's a comprehensive summary of the Game of Life application requirements:\n\n---\n\n## APPLICATION OVERVIEW\n\nThis is a **gamified Conway's Game of Life** with progressive difficulty levels, resource management, and real-time pattern detection. The goal is to maximize points within time limits and Flux budget across multiple levels.\n\n---\n\n## CORE SYSTEMS AND THEIR RELATIONSHIPS\n\n### 1. **Core Simulation Engine** (simulation-engine.md)\n**Foundation of the entire application**\n- Implements Conway's Game of Life rules (born=[3], survive=[2,3])\n- Uses age-based cell tracking (0 = dead, >0 = alive with age)\n- Toroidal boundary conditions (wrapping edges)\n- Double-buffer grid with direct ref access for performance\n- **Depends on**: Canvas rendering, Audio system, User interaction\n- **Provides to**: All other systems (grid state, generation count, birth statistics)\n\n### 2. **Phase Management** (phase-management.md)\n**Central state machine controlling game flow**\n- Four phases: PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED\n- PLANNING: Place/remove cells with Flux (START button enabled when ≥1 cell)\n- COUNTDOWN: 3-2-1 countdown before simulation starts\n- RUNNING: Auto-running simulation with timer countdown, cell placement with saved Flux (add-only)\n- FINISHED: Score finalization, 2.0s before auto-advance to next level\n- **Coordinates**: Flux management, Level progression, Scoring system, UI display\n\n### 3. **Level Progression** (level-progression.md)\n**Difficulty scaling system**\n- Multiple levels with increasing difficulty\n- Default: Time increases (45s, 60s, 75s...), Flux constant at 20\n- Alternative strategies configurable: Time Only, Resource Only, Mixed, Extreme\n- Score accumulates across all levels\n- **Uses**: Auto-advance transitions, Phase management\n- **Provides**: Time limits, Flux allocation, level configs\n\n### 4. **Flux Management** (flux-management.md)\n**Resource management mechanic**\n- Initial Flux per level: 20 (configurable 5-50)\n- Cost: 1 Flux per cell placed (same in both phases)\n- Refunds: Full refund during PLANNING phase only\n- Strategic: Decide how much to use in planning vs save for play phase\n- **Integrates with**: Grid interaction, Phase management, UI HUD\n\n---\n\n## INTERACTION SYSTEMS\n\n### 5. **User Interaction** (user-interaction.md)\n**Input handling for mouse and touch**\n- Two modes: DRAW (place cells) and ERASE (remove cells)\n- Mouse down/move/up handling\n- Touch start/move/end with preventDefault\n- Coordinate conversion from screen to grid\n- **Depends on**: Simulation engine (grid dimensions), Audio system (interaction sounds)\n- **Triggers**: Canvas rendering updates\n\n### 6. **Grid Interaction** (grid-interaction.md)\n**Direct cell manipulation interface**\n- Click to place/remove cells during PLANNING phase\n- Minimum cells rule: START disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n- Cursor states: Default, Crosshair (placeable), Forbidden (Flux=0), Minus (removable)\n- Visual feedback: Ghost preview, fade-in animations, shrink animations\n- **Disabled during**: RUNNING and FINISHED phases\n\n---\n\n## VISUAL AND AUDIO SYSTEMS\n\n### 7. **Canvas Rendering** (canvas-rendering.md)\n**High-performance HTML5 Canvas rendering**\n- Dark neon theme with age-based colors\n- Age 0: Bright cyan (#00ffff), Age 1-2: React blue (#61dafb), Age 3-5: Magenta (#ff00ff), Age 6+: Deep purple (#4a00ff)\n- Glow effects: 2-15px shadow blur based on age\n- Responsive cell size: 18px mobile, 20px desktop\n- Grid lines toggleable (hidden during RUNNING, visible during PLANNING)\n- **Receives from**: Simulation engine (grid state)\n\n### 8. **Audio Sonification** (audio-sonification.md)\n**Web Audio API for real-time feedback**\n- Generation sounds: Pitch mapped to row position, intensity to birth count\n- Interaction sounds: Different tones for draw/erase\n- Waveform selection: Sine, Triangle, Square, Sawtooth\n- Volume range: 0.0-0.5 (default 0.1)\n- Lazy initialization on first user interaction (browser policy)\n- **Receives from**: Simulation engine (birth stats), User interaction (draw/erase events)\n\n---\n\n## SCORING AND DETECTION SYSTEMS\n\n### 9. **Movement Detection** (movement-detection.md)\n**Pattern classification via centroid tracking**\n- Connected component detection (8-connectivity)\n- Centroid tracking across generations (default: 5 generation history)\n- Classification:\n  - MOVER: Centroid translating (movement threshold >0.5 cells)\n  - OSCILLATOR: Centroid static, cells changing locally\n  - STATIC: Centroid static, cells unchanged\n- **Provides to**: Scoring system\n\n### 10. **Scoring System** (scoring-system.md)\n**Real-time score calculation**\n- Per-generation scoring during RUNNING phase\n- MOVER: 10 points/gen (default)\n- OSCILLATOR: 2 points/gen (default)\n- STATIC: 0 points\n- Multiplier: 1.0 (default, configurable 0.1-5.0)\n- Smooth animation with lerp (0.2s)\n- Per-level reset, high score saved to localStorage\n- **Receives from**: Movement detection (pattern classifications)\n\n---\n\n## UI AND SETTINGS SYSTEMS\n\n### 11. **UI/Overlay System** (ui-overlay.md)\n**Comprehensive interface management**\n- Cinematic intro with \"ENTER VOID\" CTA, glitch effect on title\n- Glass HUD with:\n  - Main controls: PLAY/PAUSE, STEP, RANDOM, CLEAR\n  - Interaction modes: DRAW, ERASE\n  - Status: Waveform selector, Volume slider, Generation counter\n  - Settings toggle (gear icon)\n- Settings panel: Speed, Grid size, Visuals (grid lines), Audio toggle, Expert Settings access\n- Phase status display: Current phase, timer, Flux counter\n- **Coordinates**: All systems\n\n### 12. **Expert Settings** (expert-settings.md)\n**Hidden configuration for tuning mechanics**\n- Access: Backtick key or Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\n- Configurable parameters:\n  - Movement detection: History length (3-10), movement threshold (0.1-2.0), min cluster size (1-5)\n  - Scoring: Mover points (1-100), Oscillator points (0-20), Multiplier (0.1-5.0)\n  - Level generation: Base time (10-120s), Time increment (0-60s), Base Flux (5-50), Difficulty mode\n  - Grid sizing: Mobile/desktop cell sizes\n- Persistence: localStorage with export/import JSON\n- Real-time updates with default indicators\n- **Provides to**: Multiple systems for parameter tuning\n\n### 13. **Auto-Advance Transitions** (auto-advance-transitions.md)\n**Cinematic level progression system**\n- Sequence: FINISHED display (2s) → Fade out (2s) → Interstitial (2s) → Fade in (2s) → READY\n- Black overlay with opacity animation\n- Skip mechanism: Space/ESC to skip any transition phase\n- Interstitial: \"Level X Complete\" fading out, \"Level X+1\" fading in\n- Game state reset during interstitial (Flux, Score - no carryover)\n- Edge cases: Tab switch pauses transition, last level shows victory screen\n\n---\n\n## KEY RELATIONSHIPS AND DATA FLOW\n\n```\nUser Input\n    ↓\nUser Interaction → Grid Interaction\n    ↓                     ↓\nFlux Management ← → Simulation Engine ← → Canvas Rendering\n    ↓                     ↓                ↓\nPhase Management    Movement Detection → Scoring System\n    ↓                     ↓                ↓\nLevel Progression  Audio Sonification    UI Overlay\n    ↓                     ↓\nAuto-Advance Transitions  Expert Settings (tuning)\n```\n\n---\n\n## IMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY\n\n### Core Architecture\n- **State Management**: React with useReducer for phase/flux, refs for simulation grid\n- **Rendering**: HTML5 Canvas with DPR scaling for performance\n- **Audio**: Web Audio API with lazy initialization\n- **Storage**: localStorage for high scores and expert settings\n\n### Key Features to Implement\n\n1. **Game Loop**: requestAnimationFrame-based simulation with configurable speed\n2. **Phase State Machine**: PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED transitions\n3. **Resource System**: Flux budget with strategic allocation decisions\n4. **Pattern Detection**: Connected components with centroid tracking\n5. **Scoring**: Real-time calculation based on pattern classifications\n6. **Progression**: Multiple levels with increasing difficulty\n7. **Transitions**: Cinematic fade effects between levels with skip capability\n8. **Audio**: Position-mapped pitch for births, distinct sounds for interactions\n9. **Rendering**: Age-based neon colors with glow effects\n10. **Settings**: Comprehensive UI with expert tuning panel\n\n### Technical Requirements\n\n- **Responsive**: Mobile (18px cells) and desktop (20px cells)\n- **Performance**: 60fps with 60×80 grid max\n- **Touch**: Prevent default behavior, 44px minimum touch targets\n- **Accessibility**: Skip transitions, reduced motion preferences support\n- **Browser**: Modern browsers with Web Audio API support\n\nThis is a **complex, multi-system application** requiring careful coordination between simulation, rendering, audio, input handling, state management, and UI systems. The specifications are well-defined with clear interfaces and dependencies between components.\n</task_result>","title":"Study specs directory comprehensively","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d42f8dbffexRcfuMGBTaER7I","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771183081246,"end":1771183111342}}}}
